// Hand-written subset of Apple's private CoreDevice module (Xcode 27.3, CoreDevice 699.2).
// Every declaration here was matched against the demangled export list of
// /Library/Developer/PrivateFrameworks/CoreDevice.framework and the re-exported
// CoreDeviceUtilities.framework (see ../../check-symbols.sh). The binaries carry no
// .swiftinterface. A wrong declaration fails at link time, not at run time.
//
// Rules kept here:
// - Every enum here is resilient in Apple's binary (it exports an "enum case for" symbol
//   per case). Clients of a non-frozen enum read each case's tag from that symbol at run
//   time, so a misspelled case is a link error and no tag order is baked in.
// - Classes are only called, never subclassed; protocols are only called through
//   dispatch thunks on Apple's own conforming types.
